WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.580
- [Narrator] Both NATO and Russia

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.640
have eyes on this Swedish island.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.200
Once inhabited by Vikings

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.830
and as early as the eighth century,

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.070
this piece of land is
of strategic importance.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.210
That's because it's located in the center

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.780
of the Baltic Sea and is on
NATO's European front line.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.280
But it's also the only waterway

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.830
where Russia has direct
access to the west.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.870
Gotland is just one small
part of how NATO could benefit

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.940
if Sweden and Finland
become members of the block.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.970
Both nations have said
they will take steps

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.977
to apply for membership of
the Western military alliance.

00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:34.240
- But it is a very significant shift.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.280
These are two countries that have sought

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.860
to take position of
military non-alignment.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.920
- Finish and Swedish membership in NATO

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.320
would greatly enhance the
defense of the Baltic region

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.600
and reduce the chances
of Russian adventurism

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.130
or attack across the air,
land, and sea domains

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.437
in an integrated fashion.

00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:55.990
- [Narrator] Analysts say the expansion

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.750
of the block could make NATO stronger

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.260
and affect Russia's current
strategy in Ukraine.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.430
To understand how, we need
to look at the geography

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.083
and military capabilities
of both countries.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.740
The location of both Sweden and Finland

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.950
would mean the Alliance
has significantly more land

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.830
in the east of Europe.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.720
Take Finland, for example.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.830
It has an 830-mile long border with Russia

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.100
but if we look a little closer,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.090
we can see that this
border is full of lakes

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.930
and marshland with very few roads

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.160
for military vehicles such
as tanks to travel on.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.430
Analysts say those conditions
would be beneficial

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.900
for NATO in any potential
combat situation with Russia.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.920
- From a NATO point of view,
it's a huge opportunity.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.600
So you think about combat
and Ukraine over by Kyiv,

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.340
where Russia was trying to
push down really narrow roads.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.640
That's Finland.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.130
- [Narrator] One key area for
Russia is the Kola Peninsula

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.740
where Moscow houses
sub-launched ballistic missiles

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.623
that are key to its nuclear arsenal.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.180
Currently, the only NATO
country bordering the zone

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.280
is Norway, but analysts say
if Finland joins the block,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.186
it would increase pressure on the region.

00:01:58.186 --> 00:02:01.490
- So suddenly, if Finland's
having an exercise up here,

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.510
it's not just Norwegian forces,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.770
you know, maybe a brigade or two,

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.340
now suddenly, it might be 50,000 troops.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.200
So again, Russia has to
now divert troops up there.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.580
- [Narrator] In Sweden,
Gotland is strategic for Russia

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.410
because it could be a base
to protect its naval forces

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:16.930
in the Baltic Sea.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.430
- And they would use that
as a base of operations

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.230
for amphibious assault, for land attack,

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:24.110
for air attack and for naval attack.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.800
- [Narrator] In 2017, NATO
and Sweden worked together

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.450
on a simulated mission
of a Baltic Sea attack

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.440
which Alberque said concluded the island

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.012
would be a central part
of any invading strategy.

00:02:34.012 --> 00:02:36.230
(missile blasting)

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.810
Although Finland and Sweden
have been close NATO partners

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.150
for decades and worked
on such joint missions,

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.940
they have remained militarily non-aligned.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.680
For centuries, Sweden has
largely avoided involvement

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.380
in military conflicts while
Finland stayed out of NATO

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.480
after the Alliance formed in 1949,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.290
largely to avoid provoking Russia.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.720
- So the fact that they are deciding now

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.590
to potentially join the Alliance,

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.810
I think, is very significant
and speaks to the sense

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.550
of vulnerability that countries feel

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.670
in the wake of Russia's
invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.050
- [Narrator] Russia's
invasions of Georgia in 2008

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.859
and Crimea in 2014 sounded
alarm bells in both nations

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.520
but the current war pushed them

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.052
to reconsider NATO membership.

00:03:17.052 --> 00:03:19.910
In response, Russia, which
has long stood against

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:23.064
any eastward expansion of
the block has issued threats.

00:03:23.064 --> 00:03:24.510
According to the Kremlin,

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.320
Russian President Vladimir
Putin told the Finish president

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.130
that ending the country's decades-long

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.720
non-aligned defense policy
would be a mistake for Helsinki.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.223
And Russian Deputy Foreign
Minister Alexander Grushko

00:03:35.223 --> 00:03:36.860
said that Moscow would need to take

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.380
adequate precautionary measures

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.370
if NATO were to deploy infrastructure

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.290
for nuclear weapons near Russia's borders,

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.573
including in Finland.

00:03:43.573 --> 00:03:48.573
- I think one of the reasons
that we saw the invasion

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.610
of Ukraine is because they
are not a member of NATO

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.490
and that, you know, Russia
felt that they could,

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.820
therefore, take the action they did

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.520
without incurring a
direct response from NATO.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.770
And so I think that is
something that will be playing

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:09.100
into Moscow's of strategic calculus

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.100
that once these states are, if
they become members of NATO,

00:04:14.147 --> 00:04:18.670
then it will have to take
a more indirect action.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.880
- [Narrator] The addition of
Finland and Sweden to NATO

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.970
would also enhance some
of the block shortfalls

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.620
in air defense, according to Alberque.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.600
- They do not have sufficient

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.845
vehicle-mounted air defense systems.

00:04:29.845 --> 00:04:32.820
NATO air defenses, especially in the east

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.880
are very, very weak, and again,

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.580
this is a huge capability shortfall

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.030
that NATO's attempting to address.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.640
- [Narrator] Sweden's advanced purchases

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.150
of air-launched cruise missiles

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.590
and Finland's $9.4 billion purchase

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.890
of 64 cutting edge US F-35 fighter jets

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.170
would significantly
improve NATO's air defense

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:51.773
and attack capabilities.

00:04:51.773 --> 00:04:54.390
And it could require Russia
to add countermeasures

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.330
to that potential threat, analysts say,

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.820
spreading its resources thin

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.033
while trying to establish air dominance.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.660
But some analysts also believe

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.690
that the introduction
of Sweden and Finland

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.730
into the block could
fit into a broader plan

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.530
by Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.750
to realign his forces
to different regions.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.570
- I think Russia thought a long time ago

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.920
that Finland and Sweden
would end up joining NATO.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.610
I think it helps Putin
in terms of his messaging

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:23.600
that NATO is scary so that
he can divert resources

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.393
from human development in
Russia towards military.

